WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.168 --> 00:00:01.606
- Colombia!

00:00:01.606 --> 00:00:03.231
- Colombia, food!

00:00:03.231 --> 00:00:06.059
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.309 --> 00:00:10.720
- There is no mistaking
that this is from Colombia.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.067
- Are these the colors
of the Colombian flag?

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:12.786
- Look.

00:00:12.786 --> 00:00:14.226
- Oh it is.
- There it is.

00:00:14.226 --> 00:00:16.763
- Woah, didn't see that one coming.

00:00:16.763 --> 00:00:19.409
- Oh, dude, this smells like
Guarana, the Brazilian drink.

00:00:19.409 --> 00:00:20.525
- No, it does not!

00:00:20.525 --> 00:00:21.848
- [Man] Yeah it does.
- [Woman] No, it doesn't.

00:00:21.848 --> 00:00:25.145
- It kinda tastes like
a melted shaved ice.

00:00:25.145 --> 00:00:27.102
- I love it, it's really good.

00:00:30.522 --> 00:00:31.577
- Just pull, oh, yeah.

00:00:31.577 --> 00:00:32.600
- Ow, ow.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.550
- Like a plantain pancake, almost.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.999
- It's like, they were like,
let's take all the best parts

00:00:36.999 --> 00:00:38.671
of a plantain and just like...

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.332
- Let's take the sweet
part and get rid of it.

00:00:40.332 --> 00:00:41.411
- This is substantial.

00:00:41.411 --> 00:00:42.537
If you go to a club and you're drinking,

00:00:42.537 --> 00:00:44.116
you have a couple of
these, you'll be fine.

00:00:44.116 --> 00:00:46.704
- Love plantains when they're fried once,

00:00:46.704 --> 00:00:48.726
I love 'em even more
if they're fried twice.

00:00:51.226 --> 00:00:53.225
- I kinda think it looks
like a Pokeball that was

00:00:53.225 --> 00:00:54.927
discovered by Indiana Jones.

00:00:54.927 --> 00:00:58.442
- (laughs loudly) It's an
ancient stone Pokeball.

00:00:58.442 --> 00:01:00.905
- It looks like the thing from Splice.

00:01:00.905 --> 00:01:02.690
- Also no one's seen Splice--

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:03.655
- I've never seen--

00:01:03.655 --> 00:01:06.707
- Have you seen Splice?
Have you seen Splice?

00:01:06.707 --> 00:01:09.469
- Mmm, mmm.

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.781
- On the spectrum between,
like, sweet, and cheese,

00:01:11.781 --> 00:01:13.127
it's like, smack-dab in the middle.

00:01:13.127 --> 00:01:15.928
- God damn it, Colombia,
you're just so good.

00:01:18.138 --> 00:01:19.826
- This is good 'cause it's food

00:01:19.826 --> 00:01:21.401
and also doubles as a frisbee.

00:01:21.401 --> 00:01:24.315
- This chorizo smells incredible.

00:01:24.315 --> 00:01:27.218
- Wow.
- Yup, wow.

00:01:27.218 --> 00:01:30.283
- There's so much density
of spice in that chorizo.

00:01:30.283 --> 00:01:32.303
- We don't need this bread
it's just extra carbs.

00:01:32.303 --> 00:01:34.955
- Get rid of it, we
don't need those carbs.

00:01:38.978 --> 00:01:40.081
- Is it cow tongue?

00:01:40.081 --> 00:01:41.822
- This is what they use to say, "moo."

00:01:41.822 --> 00:01:43.482
- This isn't just strips of tongue.

00:01:43.482 --> 00:01:44.597
This is an entire tongue.

00:01:44.597 --> 00:01:46.247
- No, this is an entire tongue.

00:01:46.247 --> 00:01:47.286
(squeals)

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.341
- All right.
- This is really good.

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:50.548
- It's super soft.

00:01:50.548 --> 00:01:53.399
- That is some buttery-ass tongue.

00:01:55.539 --> 00:01:56.928
- This is a giant Nutter Butter.

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:58.375
- Is this a Colombian Oreo?

00:01:58.375 --> 00:02:00.490
- I know how it's going to
break, so I want to punch it.

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:02.775
- Ooh, nice clean break.

00:02:02.775 --> 00:02:04.238
- Hahhh!

00:02:04.788 --> 00:02:07.404
- Mmmm, I really like it.

00:02:07.404 --> 00:02:08.724
- Yeah, it's really good.

00:02:08.724 --> 00:02:11.175
- Fun to eat, hard to punch.

00:02:11.175 --> 00:02:14.921
(upbeat music)

00:02:14.938 --> 00:02:17.038
- It's just so sad what's
happening over there.

00:02:17.038 --> 00:02:18.561
- Oh, yeah, mhm.

00:02:18.561 --> 00:02:20.711
(whooshing)

00:02:21.481 --> 00:02:23.197
- You don't know the half of it.

